the target language is: lps.

% Conway's Game of Life: intensional fluents over a grid, recomputed every
% cycle. The stress case.
% Source: legacy_lps1/examples/CLOUT_workshop/life.pl
%
% The grid and the neighbour arithmetic are Prolog -- findall over a list of
% offsets -- and live in the companion file life.lps
% (docs/le_lps_surface.md §7).

the maximum time is 8.

the actions are:
    *a cell* dies; known as die.
    *a cell* comes alive; known as live.

the fluents are:
    *a cell* is alive; known as alive.

the templates are:
    *a cell* is on the grid; known as cell.
    the neighbours of *a cell* are *a list*; known as adjacent.
    *a number* of *a list* are alive; known as countLivingNeighbors.
    *a cell* has *a number* living neighbours; known as aliveNeighbors.

the knowledge base life includes:

initially 2-3 is alive
    and 3-3 is alive
    and 4-3 is alive.

a cell has a number living neighbours at a time if
    the neighbours of the cell are a list
    and the number of the list are alive at the time.

0 of an empty list are alive at a time if
    the empty list is equal to [].

a number of a list are alive at a time if
    the list is equal to [a cell | a rest]
    and the cell is alive at the time
    and a second number of the rest are alive at the time
    and the number is the second number + 1.

a number of a list are alive at a time if
    the list is equal to [a cell | a rest]
    and it is not the case that the cell is alive at the time
    and the number of the rest are alive at the time.

if a cell is alive at a first time
    and the cell has a number living neighbours at the first time
    and the number < 2
then the cell dies from the first time to a second time.

if a cell is alive at a first time
    and the cell has a number living neighbours at the first time
    and the number > 3
then the cell dies from the first time to a second time.

if a cell is on the grid
    and the cell has 3 living neighbours at a first time
then the cell comes alive from the first time to a second time.

when a cell comes alive
then the cell is alive.

when a cell dies
then it is not the case that the cell is alive.
